'''Haynadur''' ([[IPA]]: /ɦaɪnadʊr/; [[Pamil language|Pamil]]: ᨎᨆᨏᨊᨆᨉᨖᨑ; [[Eradjian language|Eradjian]]: ᨆᨈᨊᨆᨋᨖᨑ, ''Ainatur''; [[Zimonian language|Zimonian]]: ᨆᨏᨊᨆᨉᨖᨑ, ''Aynadur''; [[Rubik language|Rubik]]: ᨎᨆᨈᨊᨆᨋᨖᨑ, ''Hainatur''), officially the '''State of Haynadur''', is a [[wikipedia:sovereign state|sovereign state]] in the continent of [[Pahari]] on the planet [[Basis]]. Covering an area of TBD square kilometers, the country has a population of over 33 million people, making it the ??th-most populated country in Pahari. It is a [[wikipedia:unitary state|unitary]] [[wikipedia:diarchy|diarchic]] [[wikipedia:presidential system|presidential]] [[wikipedia:republic|republic]] led by two [[Co-presidents of Haynadur|co-presidents]] who are husband and wife. Haynadur is located in [[DIRECTION Pahari]], and shares borders with [[NEIGHBOR 1]], [[NEIGHBOR 2]], [[NEIGHBOR 3]], and [[NEIGHBOR 4]]. Its capital and largest city is [[Nirjana]]. Haynadur has four cultural and linguistic regions and four official languages: [[Pamil language|Pamil]], [[Eradjian language|Eradjian]], [[Zimonian language|Zimonian]] and [[Rubik language|Rubik]]. While the [[Pamil people|Pamil]] are the largest ethnic group, they constitute a plurality. 

One of the cradles of civilization, [[Ancient Haynadur]] witnessed the earliest developments of writing, agriculture, centralized government, and organized religion over more than three millennia. Iconic monuments such as the [[Great Gaderung of Sunne]], the [[Great Gaderung of Mona]], and the [[Valley of Death]] reflect this heritage and remain important sources of both scholarly and popular interest. During the late [[Iron Age in Pahari|Iron Age]], Haynadur became the birthplace of [[Sunneism]]. 

U/C HISTORY SECTION

Haynadur is a [[wikipedia:developing country|developing country]] with the [[List of Paharian countries by GDP (nominal)|??th-largest economy in Pahari]]. 

Haynadur is highly integrated in international affairs, being a founding member of [[INTL ORG]], [[INTL ORG]] and [[INTL ORG]]. 

